OpenSSL 3.x support for ext/openssl (php-5.4)

OpenSSL 1.1 made RSA/DSA/DH/EC_KEY/EVP_PKEY/X509 opaque, and 3.0 removed the
deprecated field access macros plus RSA_SSLV23_PADDING. Rebuild the extension
against the new API:

 - pkey->type                     -> EVP_PKEY_base_id()
 - pkey->pkey.rsa/dsa/dh/ec       -> EVP_PKEY_get0_RSA()/get0_DSA()/get0_DH()/get0_EC_KEY()
 - rsa->n/e/d/p/q/dmp1/dmq1/iqmp  -> RSA_get0_key()/RSA_get0_factors()/RSA_get0_crt_params()
 - dsa->* / dh->*                 -> DSA_get0_pqg()/DSA_get0_key()/DH_get0_pqg()/DH_get0_key()
 - direct field assignment when building a key from an array
                                  -> RSA_set0_*()/DSA_set0_*()/DH_set0_*()
 - cert->name                     -> X509_get_subject_name() + X509_NAME_oneline()
 - extension->value               -> X509_EXTENSION_get_data()
 - stack-allocated EVP_MD_CTX / EVP_CIPHER_CTX
                                  -> EVP_MD_CTX_new()/EVP_CIPHER_CTX_new() + free

Patches against upstream php-5.4.45 sources.

